title: The Party Underground
subtitle: Banned in all but name, the party learns to live in secret.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 5 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 1

= The Party Underground

The state of siege still holds in Berlin. Meetings are broken up, offices searched, organisers held for weeks without charge. *Die Rote Fahne* appears when it can. Dues hardly come in at all.

[+ party_chair +] wants an apparatus: couriers, safe addresses, a treasury and district secretaries who answer to the Zentrale. The big districts say they made a revolution without secretaries and can go underground without them too.

- @apparatus: Build an illegal apparatus run from Berlin.
- @districts: Let each district organise itself in secret.
- @diamonds: Ask Moscow for money to pay organisers.

@apparatus
subtitle: The Zentrale gets a grip on the districts, and a way to reach comrades in prison.
on-arrival: {!
Q.underground_line = 1;
Q.e19_apparatus = 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) { Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 5; }
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

Every district gets a secretary chosen in Berlin and a courier route to the Zentrale. Hamburg and Bremen call it the party of the bureaucrats.

@districts
subtitle: The Left Radicals' answer: the districts are the party.
on-arrival: underground_line = 2; ultraleft_satisfaction += 8; lean_ultraleft += 2; district_hamburg_loyalty -= 4; district_bremen_loyalty -= 4

Each district goes its own way. Some are invisible to the police. Some are full of informers, and the Zentrale cannot tell which.

@diamonds
subtitle: Two funds now. Zinoviev will think we are his.
on-arrival: {!
Q.underground_line = 4;
Q.resources += 2;
Q.independence -= 6;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
!}

A courier from Moscow arrives with diamonds sewn into his coat. They are sold in Amsterdam, and the organisers are paid for a few months.
